#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK from source"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore rustup */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the Qiskit SDK from source {#install-the-qiskit-sdk-from-source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you install the Qiskit SDK from source, you can access the current "
"development version, instead of using the version in the Python Package "
"Index (PyPI) repository. You can therefore inspect and extend the latest "
"version of the Qiskit code more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create and activate a new virtual environment {#create-and-activate-a-new-"
"virtual-environment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Navigate to your project directory and create a minimal environment with "
"only Python installed in it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Rust compiler {#install-the-rust-compiler}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Rust compiler must be installed on your system to compile Qiskit. To "
"install the Rust compiler, use the cross-platform Rust installer "
"[`rustup`](https://rustup.rs/) or [another install "
"method](https://forge.rust-lang.org/infra/other-installation-"
"methods.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Follow these steps to install Qiskit:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clone the Qiskit repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change to the `qiskit` directory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Optional) If you want to run tests or linting checks, install the developer"
" requirements.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install `qiskit`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Standard install**:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install .\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Editable mode**: In this mode, you don't need to reinstall Qiskit when "
"there are code changes to the project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install -e .\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    In editable mode, the compiled extensions are built in _debug mode_ "
"without optimizations. This affects the runtime performance of the compiled "
"code. To build the compiled extensions with optimizations enabled, run the "
"following command to rebuild the binary in _release mode_:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    python setup.py build_rust --release --inplace\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    If you are working on Rust code in Qiskit, you need to rebuild the extension code every time you make a local change. In editable mode, the Rust extension is only built when the install command is run, so local changes you make to the Rust code are not reflected in the installed package unless you rebuild the extension by rerunning `build_rust` (with or without `--release`, depending on whether you want to build in release or debug mode).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"  - Read the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) to contribute to the open-source Qiskit SDK.\n"
"  - [Run your first quantum circuit](/guides/quick-start).\n"
"  - Try a tutorial, such as [Grover's algorithm](/tutorials/grovers-algorithm).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
